-- Plan: gate elimination of x5 (two gates, either value) and then of x1 (one gate) leaves, in both
-- cases, the six-vertex edge function of the vertices 0 2 3 4 6 7, whose circuits need eight gates.
-- So every AND/OR/NOT circuit has at least eleven gates, and an eleven-gate AND/OR circuit exists.
-- The gate elimination, relabeling and one-gate lemmas are those of the checked L-meta-11719 of this
-- repository (after L-meta-10500), Apache-2.0. The six-input signed live-wire search is that of the
-- checked L-meta-12232 (after L-meta-8708), with an AND/OR-only oriented variant added here.

namespace PEqualNP.Outside.L_meta_14400

namespace Six

-- The signed live-wire search and its soundness proof are those of the merged L-meta-8708 of this
